    difficulty: "Medium",
    question: "Number of Provinces\n\nThere are n cities. Some of them are connected, while some are not. If city a is connected directly with city b, and city b is connected directly with city c, then city a is connected indirectly with city c.\n\nA province is a group of directly or indirectly connected cities and no other cities outside of the group.\n\nYou are given an n x n matrix isConnected where isConnected[i][j] = 1 if the ith city and the jth city are directly connected, and isConnected[i][j] = 0 otherwise.\n\nReturn the total number of provinces.\n\nExample:\nInput: isConnected = [[1,1,0],[1,1,0],[0,0,1]]\nOutput: 2",
    answer: "DFS from each unvisited city. Each DFS call marks a connected component. Count the number of DFS calls.",
    expectedFresherAnswer: "Maintain a visited array. For each city not yet visited, DFS to mark all connected cities. Increment province count. Time: O(n²), Space: O(n).",
    minimumAcceptableAnswer: "Candidate should use DFS/BFS or Union-Find to count connected components.",
